<title>SPAIN: Spanish beets' sugar content rises to 17.3 pct avg.</title>
<headline>Spanish beets' sugar content rises to 17.3 pct avg.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average sugar content of southern Spanish sugar beets was 17.33 percent at the most recent test, slightly higher than last year's levels, the National Sugar Beet Confederation CNR told Reuters on Friday.</p>
<p>The test was conducted on July 13 and measures sugar content at the factory door for the southern harvest from the Andalusian provinces of Cadiz, Seville, Huelva, Cordoba, Jaen, Malaga, and Badajoz. The southern harvest began three weeks ago.</p>
<p>The northern harvest begins at the end of September or the beginning of October, and crop tests should be available from early September, the CNR said.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34  1 585 2167</p>
